# CODEOWNERS — required reviewers on the trust-boundary surfaces (issue #144).
#
# This repo is the normative spec + the reusable runtime every consumer
# executes. The pipeline automates merges, so the paths below get a named
# human owner: a change to spec/ rewrites the contract consumers validate
# against, and a change to .github/workflows|actions/ is code that runs
# inside every enrolled repo's CI.
#
# Enforcement note: required code-owner review activates only once branch
# protection lands (tracked in issue #126); until then this file documents
# ownership and routes review requests.

# Default owner for anything not listed below.
*                       @Axel-DaMage

# Normative spec — semver-sensitive contract surface (schema, trust ladder,
# risk taxonomy, labels, injection defense, threat model).
/spec/**                @Axel-DaMage @scanalesespinoza

# Runtime — reusable workflow_call stages and composite actions executed
# by every consumer repo.
/.github/workflows/**   @Axel-DaMage @scanalesespinoza
/.github/actions/**     @Axel-DaMage @scanalesespinoza

# Validation tooling — the local suite that CI and `npm test` trust.
/tools/**               @Axel-DaMage @scanalesespinoza
